    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598-a4">

                <pb facs="0587" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg513"/>

                <head>C.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate Tower
                                Building, St. Water Street</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Liverpool</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 3, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> The crew from the pirate Florida,
                    numbering some 30, men were landed at this port on the 16th ultimo from one of
                    the Boston steamers. They were paid off on the 20th ultimo, and a certificate
                    given them that they were to be on the steamer Rappahannock on the 10th March,
                    until which time they were to have leave of absence. I now hear that they are to
                    muster on the Rappahannock at the time mentioned, and are then to be taken on a
                    steamer to the Stonewall now in one of the Spanish ports; most likely an English
                    steamer will perform this duty. Inform Commodore Craven.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. DUDLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>H. J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Perry,</hi> Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
